message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "ReSIDS — a Resilient, Adaptive, runtime-Switchable Federated–Gossip IDS for IEC 61850 Power Systems"
abstract: >-
  ReSIDS / ereno-Adaptativo is an intrusion-detection pipeline that unifies
  centralized, federated and gossip learning in a single run with round-by-round
  mode switching, built on Flower, scikit-learn and XGBoost. This is the v1.x
  (Paper 1 / JPDC) lineage: per-attack XGBoost specialists with k-of-n decision
  fusion, runtime FL<->GL switching (a scheduled FixedArchManager; OR-fusion makes
  gossip and federated exactly equivalent), GRASP feature selection, and node-loss
  resilience. Version 1.2 adds a two-tier design: alongside the Tier-1 specialists,
  a Tier-2 protocol-specification detector learned from benign traffic only (zero
  attack examples) flags novel attacks that violate IEC 61850 invariants; Tier 2 is
  monolithic/replicated and therefore mode-independent (identical under FL and GL).
